This code initializes the SPI communication with the MCP3008 ADC, sets up a loop to read the raw ADC value every second, logs the reading with a timestamp, and handles errors at every step. It uses the pigpio library for SPI communication and ensures a clean shutdown by terminating pigpio before exiting.

To compile and run this code, you'll need to have pigpio installed on your Raspberry Pi 4 Model B. You can install it using:

```bash
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install pigpio
```

Then compile the code with:

```bash
gcc -o moisture_sensor moisture_sensor.c -lpigpio
```

And run it with the address of your DFRobot Soil Moisture Sensor v2.0:

```bash
./moisture_sensor <sensor_address>
```

Replace `<sensor_address>` with the actual address of your sensor.

