This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ to monitor two sensors: a Keyes KY-026 Flame Sensor connected to GPIO4 and an LM393-based Heat Sensor connected to an ADS1115 ADC on I2C bus 1. The flame sensor is debounced using a falling-edge interrupt, and the temperature is read from the ADC. If both a debounced flame event and a temperature above 60°C occur, the buzzer is activated for 2 seconds, and an event is logged to fire_log.txt. If only the flame is detected, "Flame detected!" is logged; if only the temperature exceeds 60°C, the temperature reading is logged. The code handles errors, releases resources on exit, and exits cleanly on SIGINT.

