This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ to interface with a Honeywell HIH-4602-A humidity sensor via an external 12-bit MCP3208 ADC on SPI0. It reads the analog voltage from the thermistor and calculates temperature using a Beta parameter equation. The relative humidity is calculated using the sensor's transfer function. If the humidity exceeds 80%, it triggers an email alert via ssmtp. Readings are logged to `humidity_log.txt` in comma-separated format.

The code uses pigpio for SPI communication, pthread for multithreading, and epoll for signal handling. It includes error handling for pigpio initialization, SPI transfer failures, and file I/O. It also cleans up resources on SIGINT/SIGTERM.

Please replace `your_email@example.com` with your actual email address and configure `smarthome@example.com` with your SMTP server details.

Note: This code assumes that ssmtp is installed and configured on your Raspberry Pi. You may need to adjust the `sendmail` command accordingly.

Also, this code does not include the `get_timestamp()` function, which you can implement using `time(NULL)` or `clock_gettime(CLOCK_REALTIME, ...)` for timestamp generation.

