This code initializes pigpio, sets up SPI communication with the MCP3008, reads the ADC value, converts it to a percentage, and logs it to a JSON file every 5 seconds. It also controls an LED based on the water level, turning it on when the level exceeds 75% and off when it drops below 70%. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals for graceful shutdown, and logs SPI transfer errors.

Please note that you need to install the pigpio library and the json-c library to compile this code. Also, ensure that the GPIO pins are correctly connected to the MCP3008 and the water level sensor.

To compile the code, use the following command:

```bash
pigpio-compile -o water_levels water_levels.c
```

Then, run the compiled binary:

```bash
./water_levels
```

The JSON file `water_levels.json` will be created in the same directory, containing the logged water level readings.

