This code snippet is a complete C program for a Raspberry Pi Zero W to monitor a potted plant using a HiLetgo Soil Moisture Sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC via SPI. It uses the pigpio library for SPI communication and handles error checking, logging, and email alerts. The program reads the moisture level every 60 seconds, logs it to `plant_data.txt`, and sends an email alert if the moisture drops below 30%. It accepts command-line arguments for configuration and handles SIGINT and SIGTERM for graceful shutdown.

