This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ to read moisture data from a Vegetronix VH400 soil moisture sensor connected to an MCP3008 ADC via SPI. It uses the pigpio library for GPIO control and SPI communication. The program samples the moisture sensor every 5 seconds, logs readings to an in-memory circular buffer, and activates a 12V water pump when the moisture reading falls below 300 (low threshold) and turns it off when the reading rises above 600 (high threshold). The program handles errors gracefully and cleans up resources on SIGINT or SIGTERM.

Please note that you need to have the pigpio library installed and properly configured on your Raspberry Pi. Also, the MCP3008's SPI configuration (CE0, MOSI, MISO, SCLK, clock speed, mode, and data size) should match your hardware setup.

