This code initializes pigpio, sets up GPIO 24 as an output for the buzzer and GPIO 8 as an output for the MQ-2 sensor's control line. It then enters an infinite loop where it reads the analog value from the MQ-2 sensor via the MCP3008 ADC every 500 ms. If the value falls below the threshold of 500, it turns the buzzer off; otherwise, it turns it on. The program also includes error handling for pigpio initialization, SPI read operations, and GPIO write operations. Upon receiving a SIGINT (Ctrl+C), it cleans up resources by terminating pigpio and exiting.

