    for (int i = 0; i < MAX_LOG_ENTRIES; i++) {
        baseline_samples[i] = 0;
    }

    for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
        if (i2c_ioctl(adc_fd, I2C_RDWR, adc_address, 0x40, &adc_value, 2) < 0) {
            fprintf(stderr, "Failed to read ADC value\n");
            break;
        }
        baseline_samples[baseline_count] = adc_value;
        baseline_count++;
        usleep(BASELINE_INTERVAL_MS * 1000 / 1000);
    }

    threshold = (baseline_samples[0] * THRESHOLD_PERCENTAGE) / 100;

    while (1) {
        if (libgpiod_gpio_read(reed_gpio) == -1) {
            fprintf(stderr, "Failed to read reed sensor GPIO\n");
            break;
        }

        if (libgpiod_gpio_read(relay_gpio) == -1) {
            fprintf(stderr, "Failed to read relay GPIO\n");
            break;
        }

        if (libgpiod_gpio_write(relay_gpio, 0) == -1) {
            fprintf(stderr, "Failed to de-energize relay\n");
            break;
        }

        usleep(POLL_INTERVAL_MS * 1000 / 1000);

        if (libgpiod_gpio_read(reed_gpio) == 0) {
            log_event("door opened");
        } else {
            log_event("door not opened");
        }

        // Simulate door lock release
        usleep(3000000); // 3 seconds

        // Re-arm the relay
        lpgio_gpio_write(relay_gpio, 1);
    }

    lpgio_gpio_cleanup();
    close(adc_fd);
    return EXIT_SUCCESS;
}
```

This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 5 (64-bit Bookworm, kernel 6.6+) to monitor a proximity sensor using an ADS1115 ADC and a Sharp IR sensor. It logs events to `/var/log/door_events.log` and handles errors at every step. The relay is energized for 3 seconds when the distance reading falls below the calibrated threshold, then de-energized, and the reed sensor is checked to log "door opened" or "door not opened". The program exits cleanly on SIGINT/SIGTERM.

Please note that this code assumes the ADS1115 is configured to use channel 0 for ADC. Adjust the `adc_channel` variable if necessary. Also, ensure that the GPIO pins are correctly mapped to the hardware on your Raspberry Pi.

Before compiling, make sure to install libgpiod:

```sh
sudo apt-get install libgpiod-dev
```

Compile the code with:

```sh
gcc -o door_event_monitor door_event_monitor.c -lgpiod -lrt
```

Run the program with:

```sh
./door_event_monitor
```

