This code sets up a Raspberry Pi Zero W to sample analog audio from an ADMP401 MEMS microphone via a 10-bit MCP3008 ADC using libgpiod v2 and spidev. It configures the SPI interface, GPIO chip, and handles the SPI and GPIO operations, including error checking and signal handling. The sample rate is 1000 Hz, and each reading is logged to 'audio_log.txt' with nanosecond timestamps. The program gracefully shuts down on SIGINT or SIGTERM signals, releasing resources and closing the log file.

