This code captures a single 1920x1080 JPEG image from a USB camera at `/dev/video0`, saves it to "image.jpg", and handles resource release on all exit paths. It uses the V4L2 API with memory-mapped (MMAP) buffers, opens the device in blocking mode, queries device capabilities, and verifies support for required features. It requests the format V4L2_PIX_FMT_MJPEG at 1920x1080 with V4L2_FIELD_NONE, requests 4 MMAP buffers, and queues each one. It starts streaming, dequeues one frame, verifies `buf.bytesused > 0`, and writes the raw MJPEG bytes directly to disk without re-encoding. The code also includes a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler to cleanly tear down streaming and release resources when Ctrl+C is pressed.

