This code sets up a GPIO-based pan-tilt system using libgpiod for PWM control. It initializes the GPIO pins, sets their modes, and configures PWM for both servos with a 50 Hz period and duty cycles between 50 and 100. The servos start at the mid-position (75). The program polls four buttons every 50 ms, adjusting the servo positions based on button presses. It handles errors and cleans up resources on SIGINT (Ctrl+C).

