This code initializes a Raspberry Pi Zero W using the pigpio library to read proximity and ambient light data from a Silicon Labs Si1145 sensor connected over I2C (bus 1) at address 0x60. It verifies the PART ID register (0x00) reads 0x45, initializes the sensor by writing to the command register (0x18), and logs readings with ISO-8601 timestamps to "biometric_log.txt" every 500 ms. If the sensor is absent or initialization fails, it prints a diagnostic to stderr and exits non-zero. If a read fails mid-loop, it logs the error and continues. The program also installs a SIGINT handler to cleanly close the I2C handle, flush and close the log file, and call `gpioTerminate()`.

