This code initializes the pigpio library, checks for the presence of the VL53L0X sensor at the specified I2C address, and configures GPIO 17 with a pull-up. It then triggers a single distance measurement on each falling edge detected on GPIO 17. The sensor's range is set, and the interrupt is polled until it's set, after which the 14-byte result block is read, and the 16-bit distance is extracted. The interrupt is cleared, and the distance is logged to 'distance_log.txt' in CSV format. The program handles errors at every step and gracefully shuts down on SIGINT.

