This code initializes a Raspberry Pi Zero W with a Silicon Labs Si1102 proximity sensor using the pigpio library over I2C bus 1 at address 0x60. It configures GPIO27 to raise an interrupt on a rising edge when proximity exceeds a configurable threshold (default 1000). The interrupt handler reads the 16-bit proximity value from registers 0x08 (high byte) and 0x09 (low byte), logs the value to 'proximity.log' with a timestamp and status ('SAFE' or 'ALERT'), and sets a flag for the main loop to continue processing. The main loop reads the proximity value from the flag and logs it accordingly. The program supports command-line arguments for I2C address and threshold, and handles SIGINT for clean shutdown. All I2C operations, GPIO setup, and file operations are checked for errors, and resources are released on all exit paths.

