This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to use the pigpio library to measure distance with an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor connected to GPIO17 (trigger) and GPIO18 (echo). It configures the trigger pin as output, the echo pin as input with a falling/rising edge alert callback, and the buzzer pin as output. It generates a 10 us trigger pulse on GPIO17, measures the echo pulse width using an interrupt handler, computes the distance in cm, and prints it to stdout every second. If the distance falls below 20 cm, it activates the buzzer on GPIO27. The program handles errors during initialization, checks all pigpio calls, and properly cleans up resources on exit, including handling SIGINT (Ctrl+C) to terminate pigpio and exit cleanly.

