This code initializes pigpio, sets up I2C communication, and continuously reads the temperature from the STLM75 sensor. It stores the readings in a circular buffer, calculates a running average, and turns on an LED when the average temperature exceeds 28.0 °C. The program handles errors, cleans up resources on exit, and responds to SIGINT and SIGTERM signals for clean shutdown.

