This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to stream live temperature and humidity data from a Sensirion SHT40 sensor connected via I2C bus 1 at address 0x44 to a local HTTP web server listening on port 8080. It uses the pigpio library for I2C communication and the socket library for HTTP server functionality. The code includes error handling for I2C communication, including sensor-absent and bus-error cases, with up to 3 retries, and ensures clean resource release on all exit paths, including SIGINT and SIGTERM signal handling.

To compile this code, you'll need to have pigpio installed. You can install it using:

```bash
sudo apt-get install pigpio
```

Then, compile the code with:

```bash
gcc -o stream_data stream_data.c -lpigpio -lsocket -lnsl
```

Run the compiled binary:

```bash
sudo ./stream_data
```

Make sure to adjust the I2C bus and sensor address according to your setup.

