This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to monitor a Bosch BMP280 pressure sensor over I2C-1 at address 0x76. It verifies the chip ID at register 0xD0, reads the calibration block at register 0x88, and applies the Bosch compensation formulas. It configures the control register (0xF4) for 1x oversampling on temperature and pressure in forced mode (0x27), triggers a measurement by writing the forced mode bits (0x01) each loop, and waits about 10 ms for conversion completion before reading 6 bytes of raw data from register 0xF7.

The program samples every 2 seconds and logs timestamped pressure threshold breaches (above 1020 hPa or below 980 hPa) to `pressure_log.txt`. It handles I2C errors gracefully with up to 3 retry attempts that re-open the bus and re-verify the chip ID. Signal handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM are used to shut down cleanly, closing the I2C handle and calling `gpioTerminate()` on all exit paths.

