This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ to control a solid-state relay on GPIO17, modulating a resistive heater to maintain a target temperature read from a MAX31855 thermocouple amplifier over the hardware SPI peripheral. It logs temperature and PWM duty cycle to `heater_log.csv` with ISO-8601 timestamps, implements a PI controller with anti-windup and a safe maximum duty cycle of 80%, handles SPI read failures and MAX31855 faults, and provides graceful shutdown handling. The target temperature defaults to 25.0°C.

