This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to read ambient light from a BH1750 sensor using the i2c-dev interface. It reads the raw light value every second, converts it to lux, and stores the last 60 readings in a circular buffer. The average lux is then used to control an LED on GPIO17 (BCM numbering) via sysfs GPIO, blinking it at a rate proportional to the average lux. The blink pattern is a 50% duty cycle square wave. The program handles I2C read errors, cleans up resources on exit, and uses signal(SIGINT) for graceful shutdown.

