This code initializes the GY-45 MMA8452Q accelerometer over I2C on a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B, verifies its identity, and sets it to active mode. It continuously polls the accelerometer, computes the tilt angle of the X-axis relative to gravity, and logs the raw 12-bit X, Y, Z values to `fall_log.txt` when the absolute tilt angle exceeds 45 degrees. The program handles I2C syscall failures and exits gracefully on errors. It also sets up a SIGINT/SIGTERM handler to close the I2C file descriptor and the log file before exiting.

