This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 4 Model B to act as a musical doorbell. It uses the pigpio library for hardware PWM control of a piezo buzzer connected to GPIO18. The button on GPIO17 is used to trigger the melody playback, with an internal pull-up and active-low logic. The melody is stored in a lookup table `MELODY_TABLE`.

The interrupt handler `button_isr` checks for button presses every millisecond, debouncing with a 50ms gap. When the button is pressed, it toggles the `playing` flag to start or stop the melody playback.

The main loop runs indefinitely, checking for button presses. A SIGINT (Ctrl+C) or SIGTERM signal triggers a clean shutdown by calling `gpioTerminate`.

Please ensure that the necessary permissions are set for pigpio to access the GPIO pins.

