This code sets up a Raspberry Pi 3 Model B+ to monitor an active-high digital output from a SW-420 vibration sensor connected to GPIO17 (physical pin 11). It uses libgpiod for GPIO control and handles both rising and falling edges with a configurable poll timeout. The program logs every edge event to a file named `vibration_events.log` with ISO-8601 timestamps and raw values (0 or 1).

The code also implements a basic earthquake early-warning simulation using a sliding window of the last 5 events. If 3 or more of them read HIGH, it prints an "EARTHQUAKE ALERT" message with the timestamp to the console.

The program handles errors for libgpiod calls and system calls, logs file open/write errors, and ensures the log file is flushed or fsynced after each write. It also sets up SIGINT and SIGTERM signal handlers to cleanly exit the main loop and release resources.

