This code uses libgpiod to interface with the GPIO pins on a Raspberry Pi Zero W. It monitors a KY-026 flame sensor connected to GPIO17 (active-low), activating a buzzer on GPIO18 and an LED on GPIO23 when a flame is detected. The sensor reading is debounced with a 50 ms interval. Each flame detection event is logged to `flame_log.txt` with a timestamp. The program handles SIGINT and SIGTERM signals for graceful cleanup, closing all GPIO lines and the log file before exiting.

