This code sets up an interrupt-driven HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor measurement system on a Raspberry Pi Zero W using the pigpio library. It sends a 10 µs trigger pulse every 200 ms, measures the echo pulse width using interrupt callbacks, and logs valid distance measurements in centimeters with nanosecond-precision timestamps to `distance_log.txt` in CSV format. The shared pulse-timing variables are protected with a mutex, and the program handles various error conditions, including pigpio initialization failure, file open failure, invalid pulse widths, and sensor timeouts. The SIGINT handler allows for graceful termination and cleanup.

