This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up I2C communication with the LIS3DH accelerometer, configures the sensor for a 100 Hz data rate and ±2g full scale, and continuously reads acceleration data. It implements a basic fall detection system that triggers a buzzer when the acceleration magnitude drops below 0.2g (fall) and exceeds 1.5g (impact). The buzzer is activated for 1 second on impact. The program accepts optional command-line freefall and impact thresholds, handles I2C communication failures with up to 3 retries, and performs graceful cleanup on SIGINT. It also handles sensor absence and bus errors robustly, ensuring resources are released on every exit path.

