This code initializes the pigpio library, sets up GPIOs for the relay and the TTP223 sensor, and enters a loop that polls the sensor every 50ms. If the sensor detects a touch, it toggles the relay state. If the sensor remains HIGH for more than 10 seconds, the relay is toggled OFF and remains that way until the sensor is released. The program also handles errors and cleans up resources in the `main()` function after exiting the loop. Signal handlers are set up to allow the program to exit cleanly via SIGINT (Ctrl+C) or SIGTERM.

