This code sets up a closed-loop flow control system for an ASCO RedHat 8210 series proportional solenoid valve using the pigpio library. It reads flow rate from a YF-S201 flow sensor via an interrupt-driven, rising-edge pulse counter on GPIO 24, and adjusts the valve's PWM duty cycle to maintain the target flow rate. The target flow rate is provided as a command-line argument, validated, and used in the proportional control algorithm. The system logs timestamp, flow rate, and valve position to `flow_log.csv` every 100 ms. It handles errors, gracefully shuts down on SIGINT and SIGTERM, and cleans up resources before exiting.

