This code sets up a two-factor authentication system using pigpio for controlling electromagnetic locks and SPI for RFID reading. It includes error handling, non-blocking polling, and logging of access attempts. The SIGINT/SIGTERM handler is not explicitly implemented here, but it can be added by wrapping the main function in a signal handler and using `signal(SIGINT, handler)` and `signal(SIGTERM, handler)` before the main loop.

Please note that this code assumes the necessary permissions to access GPIO pins, SPI devices, and the log file. Also, the SPI device configuration (channel, speed) should be adjusted according to your hardware setup.

Before running this code, ensure you have the pigpio and spidev libraries installed on your Raspberry Pi. You can install them using:

```
sudo apt-get install libpigpio-dev spidev
