This code sets up a PID controller for two DC motors driven by L298Ns using libgpiod for GPIO control and software PWM. It includes encoder reading via edge events in separate threads, PID calculation, and motor control. The control loop runs indefinitely, stopping on SIGINT or SIGTERM. The code also logs motor speeds and PID components to `motor_log.csv`. Make sure to install libgpiod before compiling.

